Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.88,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一个问题永远不够\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}One question is never enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.20,0:00:04.55,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,现实中的分析者会自适应地问很多个\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Real analysts ask many, adaptively,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.55,0:00:07.30,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个都是看了前面的答案才选的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}each chosen after seeing earlier answers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.62,0:00:10.32,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,比如某个桶冒出尖峰，就放大看看\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Maybe you spot a spike in one bin, and zoom in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.57,0:00:12.57,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原文的定理 1 处理的就是这个\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The paper's Theorem 1 handles this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.89,0:00:14.98,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,看整份 transcript（交互历史）\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Write the probability of the whole transcript as a product, step by step.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.98,0:00:17.07,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,把它的概率一步一步写成乘积\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Write the probability of the whole transcript as a product, step by step.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.39,0:00:21.70,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,分析者怎么选下一个问题，在两个世界里都一样\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The analyst's choice of the next question is the same in both worlds,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.70,0:00:25.76,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以在比值里会约掉，每个答案只剩一个拉普拉斯比值\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so in the ratio it cancels, leaving one Laplace ratio per answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.08,0:00:30.64,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,懂强化学习的话，这就是算轨迹概率比时的那个 trick\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}If you know reinforcement learning, this is the trajectory-ratio trick:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.64,0:00:35.85,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,凡是两个世界里相同的都约掉，每一步的对数比值相加\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}whatever is identical in both worlds cancels, and the per-step log ratios add up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.08,0:00:39.97,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以隐私损失会累加，ε 就像一笔隐私预算，privacy budget\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}So privacy losses add up, and ε behaves like a budget.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.29,0:00:44.23,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个答案花掉一部分；一旦花完，管理者就不答了\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each answer spends part of it; once it is spent, the curator stops.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.55,0:00:46.93,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这就回应了 Dinur 和 Nissim\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That is the answer to Dinur and Nissim:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.93,0:00:50.82,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,预算让提问的上限明确、可度量\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}the budget makes the limit on questions explicit and measurable.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.37,0:00:54.78,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,现在你可以自己算算，实打实能省多少\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}You can now compute a real saving yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.10,0:00:58.72,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,暂停一下：直方图有 d 个桶，总预算是 ε\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pause: a histogram with d bins, total budget ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.04,0:01:03.14,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶单独算一个 counting query（计数查询），预算平分\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Treat each bin as its own counting query and split the budget evenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.46,0:01:05.34,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶要加多大的噪声？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}How much noise does each bin get?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.18,0:01:22.86,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶分到 1/d 的预算，噪声尺度就是 d/ε\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each bin gets 1/d of the budget, so noise of scale d/ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.18,0:01:26.40,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,把整个直方图当成一个敏感度为 2 的 query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Treated as one query with sensitivity 2,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.40,0:01:29.06,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶就都是 2/ε，不管 d 是多少\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}each bin gets 2/ε, whatever d is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.38,0:01:31.50,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,早先那个框架分析得更细\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The earlier framework's sharper
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.50,0:01:35.66,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,把噪声降到大约根号 d，但还是随 d 增大\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}analysis got this down to about √d, but it still grew with d.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.00,0:01:39.37,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,敏感度的用处远不止 counting query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Sensitivity reaches far beyond counts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.69,0:01:41.46,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原文举了三个例子\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Three examples from the paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.77,0:01:47.02,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第一，想象一个社交网络，每条可能的边都是数据库里的一条记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}First, picture a social network where each possible link is one row of the database.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.34,0:01:50.19,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,至少要切断多少条边，才能把网络一分为二？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}How many links must you cut to split the network in two?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.51,0:01:55.68,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这个最小割在改动一条边时最多变化 1，所以敏感度是 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That minimum cut moves by at most 1 when one link changes, so it is 1-sensitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.00,0:02:00.79,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一般来说，凡是“至少要改动多少条记录才能让某件事成立”\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}In general, any question of the form, how many rows would you have to change to make
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.79,0:02:02.74,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这类问题，敏感度都是 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}something true, has sensitivity 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.98,0:02:07.48,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第二：如果一个算法读到每条记录的概率都很小\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Second: if an algorithm that rarely looks at any particular row,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.48,0:02:10.57,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,比如只看一个小规模随机样本\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}like one working from a small random sample,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.57,0:02:13.66,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,而且大多数时候能把 f 近似到 σ 以内\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}approximates f to within σ most of the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.66,0:02:17.38,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对每个数据库都如此，那么 f 的敏感度最多是两倍 σ\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}on every database, then f has sensitivity at most 2σ.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.70,0:02:18.98,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这就是引理 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That is Lemma 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.03,0:02:22.47,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第三，答案不一定是一个数：一个排名、一个集合\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Third, the answer need not be a number: a ranking, a set,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.47,0:02:26.03,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一个比特串，凡是答案之间能定义距离的都行\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}a string of bits, anything with a distance between answers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.35,0:02:31.14,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,选中某个输出的概率，随它到真实答案的距离呈指数衰减\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pick an output with probability that decays exponentially with its distance
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.14,0:02:35.23,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,速率是 ε 除以两倍敏感度\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}from the true answer, at a rate of ε over twice the sensitivity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.55,0:02:40.10,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对比特串来说，这就是每个比特以略低于 1/2 的概率翻转\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}For bit strings, that flips each bit with probability a little below 1/2:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.10,0:02:42.78,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,又是 Warner 的硬币，这次用在了答案上\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Warner's coin again, applied to the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.62,0:02:47.34,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,来看这篇 paper 的最后一部分\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Now the last part of the paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.66,0:02:52.60,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,统计学家和数据挖掘研究者传统上偏爱非交互式模型\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Statisticians and data miners traditionally prefer the non-interactive model:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.60,0:02:56.97,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,数据只做一次隐私处理，发布出去，谁想算什么都行\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}sanitize the data once, publish it, and let anyone compute anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.29,0:02:59.14,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,在这个定义下，行得通吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Can that work under this definition?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.38,0:03:01.26,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原文证明了一个惊人的局限\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The paper proves a striking limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.58,0:03:03.50,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,假设每条记录都是一个 d 位的比特串\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Let each row be a string of d bits.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.82,0:03:06.64,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这里有一族简单的 counting query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Here is a family of simple counting queries:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.64,0:03:10.09,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,给每条记录一个自己的 mask（掩码），也就是一组比特位置\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}give each row its own mask, a subset of bit positions,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.09,0:03:14.19,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,统计有多少条记录在自己的 mask 内有奇数个 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and count the rows with an odd number of ones inside their mask.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.51,0:03:16.60,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个 query 的敏感度都是 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each query has sensitivity 1,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.60,0:03:22.15,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以交互式的管理者回答任意一个，噪声只要 1/ε 左右\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so an interactive curator can answer any one of them with noise of about 1/ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.38,0:03:25.67,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,但一次性发布必须同时为所有 query 做好准备\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}But a one-shot release must prepare for all of them at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.99,0:03:29.51,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,定理 3 表明，对其中至少 2/3 的 query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Theorem 3 shows that for at least 2/3 of these queries,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.51,0:03:31.62,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,两个随机数据库的发布结果几乎一样\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}the release looks almost the same
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.62,0:03:36.04,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一个里每条记录的 mask 内都有偶数个 1，真实答案为 0\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}for a random database where every row has even parity, true answer 0,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.04,0:03:39.17,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,另一个里每条记录都有奇数个 1，真实答案为 n\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}as for one where every row is odd, true answer n.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.49,0:03:41.84,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这已经是最大的差别了\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The most extreme difference possible,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.84,0:03:46.03,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,却根本看不出来，除非数据库大到指数级\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and it cannot be seen, unless the database is exponentially large:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.03,0:03:50.35,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,粗略地说，每条记录每多 4 个比特，需要的记录数就翻一倍\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}roughly, every 4 extra bits per row doubles the rows you would need.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.60,0:03:51.64,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,暂停想一想\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pause and ponder:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.64,0:03:56.42,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,分析者就不能把这些 query 也都拿去问交互式的管理者吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}couldn't an analyst just ask the interactive curator all of these queries too?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.27,0:04:08.97,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,不行：预算会用光\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}No: the budget would run out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.29,0:04:14.50,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,管理者只需回答真正有人问的那几个问题，而且是后来才选的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The curator only has to answer the few questions someone actually asks, chosen later.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.82,0:04:17.78,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,发布的结果没法预知会是哪几个\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}A published release cannot know which few those will be,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.78,0:04:20.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以必须同时为所有问题做好准备\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so it must be ready for all of them at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.43,0:04:21.88,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一次性发布就败在这里\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That is where it breaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.93,0:04:23.81,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,证明思路用到两个事实\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The proof idea uses two facts.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.13,0:04:28.53,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,隐私迫使发布结果对每种可能的记录几乎一视同仁\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Privacy forces the release to treat every possible row almost alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.85,0:04:33.41,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,而随机的 mask 把所有记录分成两半，像椒盐一样混在一起\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}And a random mask splits all rows into two halves mixed like salt and pepper,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.41,0:04:36.55,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以偶数那一半就像对全体的随机抽样\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so the even half is like a random poll of everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.87,0:04:40.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,接着是链式 trick：从完全随机的记录出发\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Then the chain trick: start from completely random rows,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.11,0:04:42.54,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一条一条地换成偶数记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and swap them one at a time for even ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.86,0:04:45.00,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每次替换对输出几乎没影响\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each swap barely moves the output,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.00,0:04:48.64,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,除非 n 极大，n 次加起来也几乎没影响\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and unless n is huge, all n swaps together barely move it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.96,0:04:53.31,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,换成奇数记录也一样，所以两个数据库看起来都像随机记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The same goes for odd rows, so both databases look like random rows.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.55,0:04:58.25,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Warner 的硬币，也就是随机响应：每个人自己扰动自己的记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Warner's coin, randomized response, where each person scrambles their own
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.25,0:05:01.78,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以谁手里都没有原始数据；它的局限还要更大\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}row so nobody holds the raw data, is even more limited.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.10,0:05:06.02,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,命题 2：即使每条记录都用同一个 mask，对大多数 mask\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Proposition 2: even when every row uses the same mask,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.02,0:05:11.81,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,它也估计不出奇数记录的个数，除非 n 大到指数级\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}for most masks it cannot estimate the odd count unless n is exponentially large.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.05,0:05:13.65,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,注意量词\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Careful with the quantifiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.95,0:05:18.26,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对任意单个、事先已知的 query，一次性发布都能答好\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}For any one query known in advance, a one-shot release can answer it well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.58,0:05:22.48,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,除非数据库大到指数级\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}What is impossible, unless the database is exponentially large,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.48,0:05:25.51,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,单单一次发布不可能既满足差分隐私，又答好其中的大多数\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}is one private release that answers most of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.83,0:05:27.22,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,结论是：想对各种问题都灵活地答准\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The lesson: for broad,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.22,0:05:31.51,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,又要强隐私，就让可信的管理者留在回路里\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}flexible accuracy with strong privacy, keep the curator in the loop.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.15,0:05:35.69,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,回到地图上，看看这篇 paper 的后续发展\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Back to our map, to see what grew from this paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.01,0:05:40.21,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,同一年，Dwork 的特邀论文标题就叫《Differential Privacy》\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The same year, in an invited paper titled simply Differential Privacy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.21,0:05:43.07,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,给这个领域起了沿用至今的名字\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Dwork introduced the name the field still uses.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.39,0:05:46.27,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,同年她还与 Kenthapadi、McSherry\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Another 2006 paper, with Kenthapadi,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.27,0:05:48.43,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Mironov 和 Naor 合写了一篇 paper\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}McSherry, Mironov and Naor,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.43,0:05:50.20,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,引入了一个极小的松弛量 δ\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}added a tiny slack, δ.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.52,0:05:54.04,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,还记得高斯噪声的比值在尾部冲出带外吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Remember the Gaussian whose ratio escaped the band in the tails?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.36,0:05:58.13,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,δ 替罕见的尾部买单，让钟形曲线回来了\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}δ pays for those rare tails, and lets the bell curve back in.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.37,0:06:00.99,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,给每个可能的答案打分\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Scoring every possible answer became McSherry and Talwar's exponential mechanism.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.99,0:06:03.62,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,后来成了 McSherry 和 Talwar 的指数机制\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Scoring every possible answer became McSherry and Talwar's exponential mechanism.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.93,0:06:07.58,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,隐私预算发展成了一套组合定理\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The privacy budget grew into a theory of composition,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.58,0:06:10.89,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Dwork、Rothblum 和 Vadhan 还带来了一个惊喜\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}with a surprise from Dwork, Rothblum and Vadhan:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.89,0:06:12.13,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,只要允许那个极小的 δ\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}allow that tiny δ,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.13,0:06:17.01,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,k 个问题的总损失就只按根号 k 增长\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and the total loss of k questions grows only like the square root of k.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.25,0:06:21.13,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Warner 的硬币，也就是第 4 节里证明局限最大的那个模型\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Warner's coin, the model Section 4 showed is most limited,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.13,0:06:24.28,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,正是今天所说的本地化差分隐私\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}is what we now call local differential privacy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.28,0:06:27.55,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Google 用在 Chrome 浏览器里，苹果用在 iPhone 上\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}used by Google in Chrome and by Apple on iPhones.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.87,0:06:29.47,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,为什么偏偏是最弱的模型？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Why the weakest model?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.52,0:06:33.87,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原始数据不用托付给任何人；用户上百万时\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Nobody has to be trusted with the raw data, and with millions of users,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.87,0:06:36.62,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,几个简单的统计量也扛得住噪声\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}a few simple statistics can afford the noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.87,0:06:40.02,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,2016 年，Abadi 和合作者让深度网络在差分\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}In 2016, Abadi and colleagues made it practical
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.02,0:06:42.23,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,隐私下也能真正训练起来\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}to train deep networks privately:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.23,0:06:45.58,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,把每个样本的梯度 clip（梯度裁剪）到一定大小以内\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}clip each example's gradient, like our income cap,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.58,0:06:48.87,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就像我们的收入上限，从而限制了敏感度\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}which bounds its sensitivity; add Gaussian noise;
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.87,0:06:51.89,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,加上高斯噪声；并在成千上万步里跟踪预算\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and track the budget over thousands of steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.21,0:06:55.75,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,用病人数据训练模型的话，这就是你的切入点\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}If you train models on patient data, this is your entry point.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.07,0:06:58.40,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,训练好的网络不过是又一个 f(x)\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}A trained network is just another f(x),
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.40,0:07:01.86,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,问“某个病人在不在训练集里”的攻击\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and attacks that ask whether a patient was in the training
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.86,0:07:04.36,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就是我们那个做减法的攻击的放大版\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}set are our subtraction attack, scaled up.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.60,0:07:06.27,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,还有 2020 年的人口普查\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}And for the 2020 census,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.27,0:07:11.71,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,美国人口普查局用差分隐私保护了公开发布的表\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}the US Census Bureau protected its published tables with differential privacy;
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.71,0:07:15.48,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,只有少数几项，比如各州人口，是精确的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}only a few counts, like state populations, were exact.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.80,0:07:17.49,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,但这是一次性发布\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}But that is a one-shot release.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.81,0:07:20.43,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,暂停想一想：这和第 4 节的结论矛盾吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pause and ponder: does Section 4 forbid it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.27,0:07:30.20,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,不矛盾\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.25,0:07:34.43,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,人口普查局的发布，是针对一组事先选定的固定表格量身定制的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The Census tuned its release for a fixed set of tables chosen in advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.75,0:07:38.24,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第 4 节排除的只是这样一种发布\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Section 4 only rules out one release that is accurate
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.24,0:07:40.81,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对一大类问题里的大多数都答得准\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}for most of a huge family of questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.15,0:07:49.71,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,我们来回顾一下。第一，隐私指的是：改动任何一个人的记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Let's recap. One: privacy means changing any one person's row changes
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.71,0:07:54.07,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,任何输出的概率之比最多是 e^ε\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}the probability of any output by at most a factor of e^ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.39,0:07:56.51,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第二，一个 query 的敏感度\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Two: a query's sensitivity is the most one row can change its answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.51,0:07:58.64,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就是一条记录最多能让它的答案变化多少\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Two: a query's sensitivity is the most one row can change its answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.96,0:08:03.27,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第三，尺度为敏感度除以 ε 的拉普拉斯噪声\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Three: Laplace noise with scale sensitivity/ε makes it private,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.27,0:08:06.55,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就能让它满足差分隐私，数据库再大，误差也不会变大\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}with error that does not grow with the database.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.87,0:08:09.49,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第四，一张满足差分隐私的公开表\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Four: one private published table cannot
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.49,0:08:14.46,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,答不好大多数简单的奇偶 query，除非数据库大到指数级\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}answer most simple parity counts unless the database is exponentially large.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.10,0:08:18.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,最后留几道题给大家自测，每道题后面都可以暂停一下\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Some questions to test yourself; pause after each.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.43,0:08:23.18,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第一题：n 个 0 到 1 之间的数，平均值的敏感度是多少？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}First: what is the sensitivity of the average of n numbers between 0 and 1?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.43,0:08:36.21,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第二题：在一个医学影像数据集里，每个病人贡献 50 张切片\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Second: in a medical imaging dataset, each patient contributes 50 slices,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.21,0:08:39.28,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每张切片的梯度都 clip 到 C 以内\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and each slice's gradient is clipped to size C.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.60,0:08:42.59,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一个病人能让梯度之和改变多少？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}How much can one patient change the summed gradient?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.83,0:08:56.22,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第三题：为什么中位数会给拉普拉斯机制带来麻烦？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Third: why does the median give the Laplace mechanism trouble?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.54,0:08:59.96,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,答案和更多练习，都在配套笔记里\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Answers, and more exercises, are in the companion notes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.20,0:09:12.23,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,下次有人说数据集匿名化了，所以很安全，你就知道真正该问的是\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Next time someone says a dataset is safe because it is anonymized,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.23,0:09:17.54,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,用的是多大的 ε，什么才算一个人的一条记录？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}you will know the better questions: what is the ε, and what counts as one person's row?
